  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1367(b)(2) and Reg. 1.1367-2(e), when S corporation losses reduce a shareholder''s debt basis below face value, repayment in excess of the adjusted debt basis triggers gain. Mercer''s debt basis is $15,000, so repayment of $40,000 produces $25,000 of capital gain because the note is a capital asset in the shareholder''s hands.
Wrong (A): The repayment is not entirely a nontaxable return of principal. The $25,000 excess over adjusted debt basis is a taxable gain event.
