Wrong (A): S corporations do not pay estimated taxes on behalf of shareholders. The entity-level tax obligation is limited to built-in gains tax and excess net passive income tax.
Wrong (C): There is no provision for splitting estimated tax obligations between the S corporation and its shareholders. Shareholders bear the full responsibility.
