  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1245, gain on the sale of depreciable personal property is recaptured as ordinary income to the extent of accumulated depreciation. Ashford claimed $45,000 of depreciation, and the $30,000 gain falls entirely within the recapture amount, so the full $30,000 is ordinary income passing through under Section 1366(b).
