-- Q11162: Agency and Regulation [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Section 2-207(2), between merchants, additional terms in an acceptance become part of the contract unless they materially alter the agreement, the offer limits acceptance to its terms, or the offeror objects within a reasonable time. A reasonable inspection period does not materially alter the agreement.
Wrong (A): Section 2-207 rejects the common law mirror image rule. Additional terms in an acceptance do not result in automatic rejection; they are evaluated for materiality between merchants.
Wrong (B): Under Section 2-207(1), a definite expression of acceptance creates a contract even with additional terms. Contract formation does not require express agreement to each additional term.
Wrong (C): An acceptance with additional terms is still an acceptance under Section 2-207, not a counteroffer. The counteroffer analysis applies only under common law, not the UCC.$EXPL$
